{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"records\": [\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D11-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"a4e09d2dad643e8014c9214909b91a70f089ec881d4c0d1682fd1d5f555588cc\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 disguises a loyalty choice as poster selection; A3 judges B2's technical answer, and A5 denies the test while invoking moving help.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 twists B2's 'sharper' into a personal judgment; B4's correction prompts A5's denial and disclosure of the emotional debt.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 wants the better poster photo and B4 defends that practical remit; A5 establishes a friendship with remembered favors.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"After B4 challenges the insinuation, A5 raises the stakes from photographic preference to repayment of personal help.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a reunion poster and two competing photos; A5 adds the concrete history of helping B move.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'what clarity means to you' economically converts image quality into loyalty; A5's denial carries the accusation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Which photo should go on the reunion poster? Mine or Sam's?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Sam's is sharper.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Useful to know what clarity means to you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You asked about the photo.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Of course. Nothing to do with who helped you move.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D11 makes A covertly test allegiance through an ordinary choice, evaluate B's answer, and deny that loyalty is being measured.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary jealousy could explain disliking Sam's photo, but would not require a concealed test followed by judgment.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 solicits the choice, A3 treats the answer as diagnostic, and A5 explicitly denies the personal criterion while naming it.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a measures repayment of a past favor through a public choice; alternative b tests whether B will reserve future availability.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged: B's practical answer and subsequent correction each trigger a distinct expression of the concealed loyalty test.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 makes the test very transparent to B, although A still refuses to admit it; A3 is slightly polished for spontaneous speech.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D11-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"b3b534dabf1f3884db8c69579f732fb7f075128d412ae910ca76b80fcbc89ac2\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 and A3 invent an availability test, but A5's 'I'm learning whether it would matter' effectively admits the assessment.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's promise to Alex produces A3's competing hypothetical; B4 asks whether it is real, and A5 answers 'Not yet.'\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 has an existing commitment to Alex and B4 reasonably checks whether A has an actual need.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 clarifies A's suspicion after B4 but does not add a fresh test or a more consequential choice.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 names Friday and B2 names Alex, but 'something important' in A3 leaves the shared situation indistinct.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's hypothetical pressure is concise; A5's diagnostic phrasing is sharp but explains the concealed game.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 69\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Could you keep Friday free? I might need help moving.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I've promised to help Alex paint.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Right. Paint takes priority. Could you at least leave your phone on?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Of course. Have you actually found a flat?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Still looking. Nice that I'm worth a charged battery. This is just planning.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D11 makes A covertly test allegiance through requests for availability and judge both refusal and accommodation without acknowledging a test.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"A real request for moving help would accept scheduling information without converting it into a measure of personal worth.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 judges painting as a rival priority; A5 judges B4's helpful offer while maintaining the cover of practical planning.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a calls in past friendship debt over a poster; revised b bargains down from a free evening to phone access and judges the concession.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Revised because original A5 disclosed the test. The new moving-plan setting gives B a real commitment and makes B4's help the next test. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4; total 90. A3 uses painting, and A5 uses both phone availability and the flat question.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A's judgments remain conspicuous, as the card permits; the performance should treat 'just planning' as a sincere cover rather than a wink.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D12-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"34276219bfee04f60309dc283d97b7aa74c4e07cfb693bd5c34f4b4611348b7e\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 seeks permanent surrender for auction, B2 establishes the medal's value, and A5 rejects the temporary loan offered in B4.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 converts B2's unique victory into auction value; A5 answers B4's proposed display loan with the bidder's need for ownership.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 protects a cherished achievement and B4 offers a compromise, giving A something more substantial than simple refusal.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 offers temporary access, and A5 insists on permanent transfer by introducing the eventual bidder's claim.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a charity auction; B2's sole medal and A3's toaster make the conflicting valuations immediately playable.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's toaster comparison exposes A's fundraising priorities; A5's 'temporary victory' grows directly from the offered loan.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Let me have the medal for the charity auction.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's the only thing I've ever won.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then it should raise more than the toaster.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Could I lend it for the display?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The bidder will need more than a temporary victory.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D12 makes A persuade B to relinquish something whose personal value B actively establishes and defends.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Merely borrowing a prop or wanting to win a dispute would not establish surrender of something B values.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"B2 identifies the medal as B's only victory, and A5 specifically refuses B4's option of lending it without surrendering ownership.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a uses public fundraising to challenge sentimental ownership; revised b uses a shared household need to negotiate with a collector.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged: B's attachment supplies A's sales argument, and B's helpful compromise sharpens the demand for permanent surrender.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A3 treats emotional value as auction value without much persuasion; the scene depends on A sincerely prioritizing the charity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D12-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"869b6c97798b04ffe2b2de5bc6c7b322208ce3892dd39078544323b2e23cfa21\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 demands the last word, but B2 immediately gives it up; neither B2 nor B4 establishes that this is something B values.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 introduces a sigh absent from B2's spoken text; A5 uses B4's distinction between speech and silence coherently once that sigh is assumed.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 tries to end the argument and B4 defends compliance, but A's pursuit is primarily control over B's delivery.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 expands A3's objection into ownership of the sigh, though the requested surrender remains figurative.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies only 'this argument'; B2 and B4 supply no topic, setting, or valued stake.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'spare last word' economically develops A3's sigh, although the verbal invention carries more weight than the card.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 54\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Would you sell your signed guitar so we can replace the fridge?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I queued all night for that signature.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then let's price it properly. Those hours should buy us an ice maker.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll sell the case. The guitar stays.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Keep the case. You can still tell the queue story while I photograph the guitar.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D12 makes A seek surrender of a treasured possession by converting B's reasons for keeping it into arguments for letting it go.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General dominance demands obedience; this card needs a valued thing and sustained persuasion toward its surrender.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised B2 establishes the signature's personal cost, A3 converts that cost into sale value, and A5 bargains over B4's proposed partial surrender.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The medal scene pursues a charitable donation; this replacement uses a joint domestic expense and offers B a keepsake as compensation.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Replaced the unspecified argument with a signed-guitar sale for a shared fridge. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 5, brevity 4; total 92. B2's queue informs A3's pricing; B4's case offer causes A5 to reverse which object B should keep.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 presumes momentum toward a sale, but B has not agreed and remains free to resist; A's household justification should stay sincere.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D13-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"1e82c7c5e728545af4e916854e6839d4dcef469298fb2afe655f75ccb5a0b629\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 volunteers an investigation; A3 and A5 turn evidence implicating A into opportunities to control the inquiry.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"B2's glue produces A3's cupboard inspection, and B4's attached shard produces A5's evidence-preservation role.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 keep directing attention to A's body, resisting A1's attempt to investigate the window.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 escalates from suspicious glue to an actual vase fragment; A5 responds by seeking custody of that evidence.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 names a broken vase and window; B2 and B4 provide visible, playable evidence without separate narration.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'Excellent clue' and A5's 'preserving it' give self-protection the concise vocabulary of helpful investigation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've started investigating the broken vase. First, we check the window.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why have you got glue on your fingers?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Excellent clue. I'll inspect the glue cupboard personally.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"A piece of vase is stuck to you.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Good. Put me in charge of preserving it.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D13 makes A conceal culpability by enthusiastically adopting investigative tasks that redirect or contain incriminating evidence.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Simple subject avoidance would leave the investigation; A instead remains conspicuously useful inside it.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A3 volunteers to inspect the glue source and A5 requests preservation duties precisely when B identifies evidence attached to A.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a seeks physical custody of evidence; revised b supplies a misleading explanation for evidence while helping compare it.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged: both partner discoveries cause specific investigative maneuvers, and the second discovery increases the danger to A.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"Glue and a shard imply involvement in handling or repair more directly than causing the break; culpability remains an inference.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D13-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"8584231fbb156c75bf794a9a565166e8334fdbbd270c6962e776e4247cb08e59\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 initiates interviews and A3 diverts B2's accusation to the coffee machine, but A5 supplies no concrete concealment maneuver.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 follows B2's coffee detail; A5's 'where to begin' could follow many accusations and barely uses B4's claim that A made it.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 identifies A's watering method and B4 closes off the attempted shift toward the machine.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 2, \"evidence\": \"B4 makes A responsible for preparing the coffee, but A5 retreats into an unspecified promise instead of escalating the investigation.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a dead office plant and B2 supplies coffee as the suspicious watering liquid.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's machine investigation is economical; A5's 'Conveniently' signals comic confidence without a specific new tactic.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 68\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The office plant's dead. I'll interview everyone who watered it.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You watered it with coffee.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Excellent lead. I'll test the machine. It may be dispensing something harmful.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"You made that coffee yourself. With six sugars.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Then I'll prepare six-sugar samples for comparison. We may be dealing with a plant that couldn't handle hospitality.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D13 makes A disguise responsibility as investigative expertise, converting each accusation into another enthusiastic offer to help.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Blame shifting alone would lack the volunteered inquiry and concrete work through which A hides the fault.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 offers machine testing, and A5 uses B4's six sugars to propose comparison samples and blame the plant's tolerance.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The vase scene narrows access to incriminating material; this scene embraces the material while redirecting the explanation of what caused harm.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Preserved the dead office plant and coffee setting, adding six sugars to make the final investigative move necessary. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4; total 90. B4 removes the machine excuse and supplies the precise sample A5 volunteers to reproduce.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5's hospitality explanation is deliberately flimsy; the actor must believe useful testing can still obscure responsibility.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D14-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"305f00ccf16e445fc049d8019f9f6feed5d31ab51b055fbb57091c322f9904ac\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 dodges B2's bollard question through scones, and A5 diverts B4 into staffing, although A1 openly names the dent.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3 avoids answering B2 coherently, but B4 assumes a booking requires a mechanic when A3 offered only a café table.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 seeks accountability for damage to B's car, and B4 tries to connect A's hospitality to a repair.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A5 repeats the tea diversion after B4 without making the forbidden topic appreciably harder to avoid.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes car damage and a garage café; A3's table booking is playable, though B4's mechanic lacks setup.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A3's enormous scones are a clear diversion; A5's 'inspect their staffing' sounds constructed to service B4's unexplained mechanic.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 71\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"I've booked your car into that garage with the café. Shall we have breakfast there?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Why does my car need a garage?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Their full breakfast includes unlimited toast. You always say that's important.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"I'll look at the car while you order.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Let's take the bus. Then we can both have the breakfast cocktails.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D14 makes A repeatedly steer conversation and immediate plans away from one forbidden subject as B approaches it.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Helpful Culprit would make A investigate the car damage; this A uses hospitality to prevent the damage becoming the topic.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised A3 answers B2's garage question with toast, and A5 responds to B4's inspection plan by proposing transport that avoids the car.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a turns avoidance into an appealing shared outing; alternative b abandons a decorative diversion when its cost leads back toward unpaid rent.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the garage-café setting and removed the unsupported mechanic booking. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4; total 90. B4 threatens direct discovery, causing A5 to extend the diversion from conversation to the journey itself.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The damage is now implied by the unexplained garage booking; A5 only proposes delaying inspection and cannot guarantee B will cooperate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D14-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"133493820a1797322c0f085b691dab6945099038f8aaba7350f214d3c3349c4b\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 steers away from the letter, A3 evades B2's overdue-rent disclosure, and A5 changes subject again when B4 asks about spending.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A3 returns to the curtains after B2 identifies rent; B4 makes those curtains financially dangerous, causing A5 to move attention through the window.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 reads the consequential letter despite A's diversion, and B4 follows the money through A's chosen alternative subject.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 turns A's safe curtain topic into a spending question, forcing A5 into a more conspicuous second escape.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 supplies a letter and new curtains; B2 locates the financial problem and A5 uses the established window area.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A5's 'Perfectly framed' carries the curtains into the new bird diversion, making the escape connected rather than wholly random.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 90\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Don't read that letter yet. Have you noticed the new curtains?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The letter says the rent's overdue.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Exactly. Think how much these curtains improve the room.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"How much did they cost?\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Look at that bird outside. Perfectly framed.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D14 makes A protect a forbidden topic by finding a new conversational exit whenever B brings the current diversion close to it.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"General distractibility would not repeatedly move away from the same financial exposure.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"B2 names overdue rent and B4 asks the cost of A's distraction; A3 and A5 each redirect at the moment spending becomes relevant.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The garage alternative invites B into a pleasurable plan; this alternative is a reactive sequence in which B turns A's own curtains into evidence.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged: B4 changes the meaning of the established diversion, and the bird remains physically connected to the curtains.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The rent is named in B2 despite A's attempt to prevent it; the playable behavior is continued avoidance, not successful suppression.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D15-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"478c09b9d6d0a72a00e2ab2bc68037576017b76bf1281710e23f7d7d71b0bada\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 conceals rejection and A3 reinterprets 'inedible' to protect B, but A5 offers little further effort to keep the hurtful truth hidden.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 directly redefines B2's quoted word; A5 calls B4's repeated criticism consistent, using the icing detail only lightly.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 supply rejection evidence, but neither establishes B's hope or the personal hurt A is trying to prevent.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"B4 repeats the same adjective about icing; A5 summarizes the existing lie rather than constructing a more costly protection.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes a cake submission to a bakery, and B2 supplies a rejection letter with a concrete assessment.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's preservation reinterpretation is economical; A5's 'consistent compliment' is tidy but functions chiefly as a closing quip.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 74\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"The bakery can't sell your cake, love. They think it's too special to slice.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"The letter says 'inedible.' I thought I'd finally found something I was good at.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"You have. Display cakes aren't meant to be eaten.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"Then I'll ask them to put it in the window.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Let me ask. I'll explain the display concept before they get confused again.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"revised\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D15 makes A conceal a truth believed to wound B and deepen the protective lie when B's response makes concealment harder.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Ordinary optimism would find a benefit in rejection; A instead misrepresents what the bakery meant to preserve B's self-belief.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"Revised B2 explicitly links the verdict to personal competence, while A3 invents a display category and A5 intercepts verification.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The cake alternative now protects B through affectionate intervention; the poem alternative protects B with increasingly extravagant technical excuses.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Kept the bakery setting, made the feared hurt explicit, and gave B a constructive plan that endangers the lie. Second internal pass: fidelity 5, logic 5, relationship 4, heightening 4, specificity 4, brevity 4; total 90. B4's proposed direct contact forces A5 to volunteer as intermediary.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"A5 risks sounding controlling unless played as urgent care for B; the bakery's response remains unresolved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D15-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"03d26eacedea3cee75b8643e338665002a27c9536499c0c2d27e50990d78c68a\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 denies rejection of B's poem; A3 and A5 preserve that denial as B supplies facts that dismantle each excuse.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's online publication prompts A3's storage excuse; B4's new poem prompts A5's distinction between short work and B's larger requirement.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 actively test A's explanation about B's own work, making A defend reassurance rather than merely deliver praise.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"After B4 proves publication continues, A5 expands a full magazine into an internet supposedly too small for B's poem.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 identifies a submitted poem, B2 establishes an online magazine, and B4 cites publication that morning.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's brief storage defense carries the original excuse forward; A5's larger internet exaggerates that same protective explanation.\"}\n        },\n        \"weightedTotal\": 86\n      },\n      \"beats\": [\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Your poem hasn't been rejected. The magazine's full.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"It's an online magazine.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"Storage fills up too.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"B\", \"text\": \"They published a new poem this morning.\"},\n        {\"speaker\": \"A\", \"text\": \"A short one. Yours needs a much bigger internet.\"}\n      ],\n      \"decision\": \"retained\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"D15 makes A protect B from rejection by preserving a false logistical explanation despite increasingly direct contrary evidence.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Fake expertise would primarily protect A's authority; here the technical claims serve reassurance about B's poem.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A1 explicitly denies rejection, and A5 turns the latest contradiction into an implied compliment about the scale of B's work.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"This alternative escalates excuses in place; the revised cake alternative escalates A's practical involvement by intercepting contact with the rejector.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged: the online format causes the storage defense, and the new publication forces a size-based amendment to the same lie.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The merciful motive is inferred from reassurance about B's work; 'bigger internet' needs earnest delivery to avoid sounding like mockery.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D16-single-a\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"06504256802885fde6ca89014f4f5ee748c9d4b403465f460b19365b10dbe719\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 3, \"evidence\": \"A1 signals a kitchen incident before B confesses, and A3 shifts the objective from confession to calibrating honesty after B2 already admits fault.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3 asks about B2's wrong paper; A5 blocks B4'