od.\",\n      \"confusableConcept\": \"Merciful lying would protect B from hurt; A's explanations instead preserve A's apparent technical authority.\",\n      \"distinguishingEvidence\": \"A5 accepts B4's engineer while instructing B to report A's invented diagnostic progress, preserving the expert performance through help.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"Alternative a incorporates professional assistance into A's supposed process; alternative b redefines physical mistakes as specialist tests.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Retained unchanged: B's constructive offer changes the tactic, and A develops the same game by claiming authorship of the handoff.\",\n      \"reservation\": \"The boiler's literal 'help' display is a comic premise; the scene works through character confidence rather than realistic diagnostics.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"D18-single-b\",\n      \"beforeHash\": \"967121f118484d406bd521400377e705972ff033cc47a96c6036c380adc929a8\",\n      \"firstPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\"score\": 5, \"evidence\": \"A1 claims a specialist tuning method; A3 and A5 confidently make obvious signs of incompetence sound intentional.\"},\n          \"responseLogic\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2's untouched strings prompt A3's preliminary wood explanation, and B4's backward instrument prompts A5's orientation test.\"},\n          \"relationship\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B2 and B4 scrutinize the treatment of B's own violin, with increasingly concrete reasons to question A.\"},\n          \"heightening\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"B4 reveals an elementary handling error, and A5 claims an even more specialized procedure to absorb it.\"},\n          \"specificity\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A1 establishes tuning B's violin; B2 and B4 give actors clear physical facts entirely through dialogue.\"},\n          \"brevityWit\": {\"score\": 4, \"evidence\": \"A3's 'We don't rush the wood' is economical; A5'